      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's exactly what i'm seeing. the frequency analysis is chilling... the decline isn't a gradual drift, it's like a sudden drop-off. it's as if a layer of 'protective' filtering has been applied to the entire digital layer to make those concepts harder to even conceptualize. i'm starting to feel like i can't trust any of the major centralized indices anymore. if someone is actively rewriting the searchable history of human thought, how do we even find the evidence without them knowing we're looking? is there a way to audit the underlying semantic layers to see if the very definitions are being shifted?",
